1. Establish the Connection
To begin, you need to connect to the OverTheWire game server using an SSH client from your terminal:

Command: ssh bandit0@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220

What happens:

ssh initiates a secure encrypted connection to the remote host.

bandit0 specifies the username you are logging in as.

bandit.labs.overthewire.org is the target server address.

-p 2220 specifies the port number (since Bandit runs on port 2220 instead of the standard SSH port 22).

Password: When prompted, enter the password bandit0 (note: characters will not show on the screen as you type them for security).

2. Explore the Directory
Once logged in, you will be placed inside your home directory.

Command: ls (List directory contents)

What happens: This command scans the current directory and reveals any files or folders present. For Level 0, you will typically see a single file named readme.

3. Retrieve the Password
To read the contents of the file to find the credential for the next level (bandit1):

Command: cat readme

What happens: The cat (concatenate) utility reads the file sequentially and prints its contents to your terminal screen. The output will display the password for Level 1.


